{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1024257-promethean-geist-and-beast-in-classic-world-of-darkness","id":1024257,"title":"Promethean, Geist and Beast in (Classic) World of Darkness","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-12-30T06:09:42-08:00","id":1024257,"title":"Promethean, Geist and Beast in (Classic) World of Darkness","content":"Retracted Statement","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11693,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/","user":"Guest","date":". 02-13-2019, 08:40 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-30T10:34:25-08:00","id":1024396,"title":"","content":"Stemming from a vague similarity of &quot;uses a given culture's version of alchemy for powers&quot;, Kindred of the East, as-is, could be a match-up with Promethean. KotE even involves a kind of pilgrimage to rise above your present state, too, though it's more about making amends with all your wickedness than becoming human again (unless, of course, you picked Flame of the Rising Phoenix for a character).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-30T11:04:38-08:00","id":1024408,"title":"","content":"Beast you could spin as a Changeling relation - souls of living nightmares that dwell in the primordial part of humanity's collective dream almost begs for a CtD connection However, a Beast's soul isn't quite like a Kithain's soul, and interacts with the world around it rather differently.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-30T11:47:13-08:00","id":1024428,"title":"","content":"I know little about Beast, but it seems to me that they would be a rather peculiar breed of Chimerical creatures. Or maybe they are related to the Fomorians in some way, or like the Fomorians, are another kind of Fae that isn't a Kithain, but is still a Changeling.<br /> <br /> Promethean can be done through a twist on the rules for Possessions. I can picture the Divine Fire in WoD as being actually a way to saw a very particular kind of spirit, and the Promethean a weird kind of Fomori/Drone/Gorgon/Kami.<br /> <br /> Geists already have a place in WoD. They are Wraiths. I don't know Wraith enough to say how to better represent Geists, but mostly a Sin-Eater would be a Possessed with a Wraith. Either way, they are already there in the same way that Changelings are.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-30T12:01:09-08:00","id":1024436,"title":"","content":"Well, I think that Geists are more Risen than Wraiths.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-30T13:30:54-08:00","id":1024482,"title":"","content":"I have flirted with the idea of Beasts in my Werewolf game. Given the negative aspects of the creatures and their monstrous spiritual affinities, I thought they fit best as powerful fomori tied closely to specific Wyrm Incarna.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3695-the-laughing-stranger","name":"The Laughing Stranger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3695_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1010"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-31T12:38:09-08:00","id":1024867,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Laughing Stranger</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1024257-promethean-geist-and-beast-in-classic-world-of-darkness?p=1024482#post1024482\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have flirted with the idea of Beasts in my Werewolf game. Given the negative aspects of the creatures and their monstrous spiritual affinities, I thought they fit best as powerful fomori tied closely to specific Wyrm Incarna.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I'd argue straight two of the tribal patrons would work as Beasts(Fenrir, Grandfather Thunder) that making them all wyrm sort of loses the point. They also seem to be much more creatures of the High Umbra than the Middle so you might get some mileage there.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-01T18:51:25-08:00","id":1025232,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1024257-promethean-geist-and-beast-in-classic-world-of-darkness?p=1024867#post1024867\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I'd argue straight two of the tribal patrons would work as Beasts(Fenrir, Grandfather Thunder) that making them all wyrm sort of loses the point. They also seem to be much more creatures of the High Umbra than the Middle so you might get some mileage there.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ehhhh... Beasts make for interesting enemies but sort of muddy the water if they aren't foes meant to be destroyed. They are tied to concepts like revulsion and hopelessness and they feed on things like greed and ruin. Not someone you want anywhere near your Caern or kin or Tellurian.<br /> <br /> Grandfather Thunder and Fenris already have children, the Garou, so unless the creatures are the Wyrm's bastards, there really isn't a good cosmological niche. Why are these possessed eldritch abomination whackos running around claiming they work for the Mother? Seems like a Wyrm trick to me.<br /> <br /> (rereads post) ...wait. Are you saying that Beasts could serve Fenris or Thunder or that the Totems <i>themselves</i> are Beasts? Option #2 seems to sell Great Fenris rather short and make even less cosmological sense.<br /> <br /> In any case, I prefer not to divide the umbra into 'high, middle and low' since that is largely mage conception of the spirit world and most werewolves know that willworkers are, at best, idiot children playing with forces beyond their control.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3695-the-laughing-stranger","name":"The Laughing Stranger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3695_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1010"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-01T21:19:05-08:00","id":1025285,"title":"","content":"I do not particularly like the Beast concept myself. It just seemed to be another &quot;Marketing: The Ploy&quot; concept that did not fly.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-02T01:58:18-08:00","id":1025341,"title":"","content":"In the XIX century there was a fad among Mages for creating Prometheans. An Awakened one is given as an example character.<br /> <br /> Beasts could be emerging servants of the Wyrm of Balance!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-02T06:58:33-08:00","id":1025415,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Laughing Stranger</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1024257-promethean-geist-and-beast-in-classic-world-of-darkness?p=1025232#post1025232\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Ehhhh... Beasts make for interesting enemies but sort of muddy the water if they aren't foes meant to be destroyed. They are tied to concepts like revulsion and hopelessness and they feed on things like greed and ruin. Not someone you want anywhere near your Caern or kin or Tellurian.<br /> <br /> Grandfather Thunder and Fenris already have children, the Garou, so unless the creatures are the Wyrm's bastards, there really isn't a good cosmological niche. Why are these possessed eldritch abomination whackos running around claiming they work for the Mother? Seems like a Wyrm trick to me.<br /> <br /> (rereads post) ...wait. Are you saying that Beasts could serve Fenris or Thunder or that the Totems <i>themselves</i> are Beasts? Option #2 seems to sell Great Fenris rather short and make even less cosmological sense.<br /> <br /> In any case, I prefer not to divide the umbra into 'high, middle and low' since that is largely mage conception of the spirit world and most werewolves know that willworkers are, at best, idiot children playing with forces beyond their control.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Beast &quot;end Game&quot; is in COD is Be Fenrir, or Wendigo, or Uktena or Gryphon. Maybe not as a Full Tribal totem but the IRL myths that lead to the Totems inspired Beast End Games.<br /> <br /> <br /> Beasts are scary big monsters, that's really the concept &quot;How can I play a Dragon, a Giant, and a Gryphon in the same party&quot; and also play crossover friendly. They are no more beholden to &quot;Feeds on Ruin' than Changelings in the WOD have to eat emotions to power themselves, or how COD Changelings are untouched by banality. Or Awakening Mages have to deal with subjective reality, or Ascension mages have to deal with the Supernal.<br /> <br /> <br /> So lets look at the WOD. You have a game that focuses on the Dreaming(Changeling) the Middle Umbra(Werewolf) the Low Umbra(Wraith) WIth the High Umbra being somewhat of the odd man out, Awakening definately makes the Astral Mage territory and Ascension is really the only one who puts much stock in it So its fairly open for use and development, and as a place of concepts they can slip readily into other lines.<br /> <br /> They are Divine monsters, the blood of gods mixing with humans to make something strange and great. Feared and worshiped.<br /> <br /> The Other Direction I might go is Beasts as Formorian Changelings but that might have too much thematic overlap with D:TF<br /> <br /> <br /> As for &quot;The spirit world isn't divided&quot; into 3 levels... That's objectively written up in Werewolf. Its not a &quot;Crazy Mage Theory&quot;. Its right tehre in the Umbra book. Werewolves can't get into the astral umbra without trouble, and have a hard time entering the deadlands.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-02T09:12:24-08:00","id":1025468,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheShadowMan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1024257-promethean-geist-and-beast-in-classic-world-of-darkness#post1024257\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Of course the (Classic) World of Darkness doesn't have Promethean, Geist and Beast lines and I was curious if anyone had an ideas for WOD versions of them, in the same way that Chronicles of Darkness has many versions of lines that appear in WOD. I did see an interesting idea on these forums once for a WOD Promethean where their meant to be in effect the replacements of Humanity, each their own &quot;Adam and Eve&quot;. I wondered if anyone had any other ideas.</div> </div> </div> </div>Are you looking to make them a supernatural full-on splat in their own right, like vampires, mages, etc.? Or are you looking for nooks and crannies in the WOD where such critters or their analogues already exist? Not that the two are mutually exclusive. But the follow-up question is definitely, as you looking for playable characters or just finding ways to expand out the the various NPC roles they already fill.<br /> <br /> For example, full on Prometheans as PCs with some adaptation of the COD mythology, roles, powers, etc. might not be served by shoehorning them into &quot;Oh mages made a lot of those in the 19th Century!&quot; because that's really not as interesting. It makes them just something tacked onto Mage and looses a lot of what makes Promethean interesting and playable. They're effectively just a type of critter that's playable like consors or familiars in an Ascension's Right Hand type of set-up. That's not how splats work. There is typically some splat compatibility where different types of the supernatural in question sync with another splat in another line (like Tremere and mages), but one line isn't just the byproduct of another.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-02T11:39:21-08:00","id":1025507,"title":"","content":"Are you aware that Prometheans <i>did</i> appear in the World of Darkness? Granted, they only appeared in the <b>Mage Storyteller's Handbook, Revised</b>, which was a book of hacks and variants; but it did include <i>the Promethean Plague</i>, a scenario set in the waning days of the Order of Reason when the predecessors of the Progenitors went wild with creating life and let loose a plague of Frankenstein monsters called \u201cPrometheans\u201d that rebelled against their creators and went on rampages.<br /> <br /> EDIT: My own take for WoD Prometheans is that they're constructs who have spontaneously Awakened \u2014 not in the Mage sense, mind you; but more in the sense of \u201cemergent intellects\u201d. A Promethean started its existence as some sort of machine: a construct that existed to serve its master and that lacked self-awareness and free will. At that stage in its existence, it wasn't a Promethean; it was just a tool.<br /> <br /> Then it encountered Prometheus, a force or entity that I view as being vaguely reminiscent of <b>Hunter</b>'s Messengers: no one has ever encountered it other than the constructs that it touches. When it touches a construct, it imbues that construct with the Spark, which in turn grants self-awareness and free will to it.<br /> <br /> A Promethean is a construct that has received the Spark.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 01-02-2017, 03:39 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-02T11:55:54-08:00","id":1025516,"title":"","content":"While they're not called geists or Sin-Eaters, <b>Orpheus</b>' projectors fill essentially the same niche: living people who have had near-death experiences and now stand with one foot in the living world and one foot in the realm of ghosts. They're about as similar to Sin-Eaters as <b>Changeling: the Lost</b>'s protagonists are to <b>Changeling: the Dreaming</b>'s protagonists.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-02T17:15:50-08:00","id":1025634,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1024257-promethean-geist-and-beast-in-classic-world-of-darkness?p=1025507#post1025507\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Are you aware that Prometheans <i>did</i> appear in the World of Darkness? Granted, they only appeared in the <b>Mage Storyteller's Handbook, Revised</b>, which was a book of hacks and variants; but it did include <i>the Promethean Plague</i>, a scenario set in the waning days of the Order of Reason when the predecessors of the Progenitors went wild with creating life and let loose a plague of Frankenstein monsters called \u201cPrometheans\u201d that rebelled against their creators and went on rampages.<br /> <br /> EDIT: My own take for WoD Prometheans is that they're constructs who have spontaneously Awakened \u2014 not in the Mage sense, mind you; but more in the sense of \u201cemergent intellects\u201d. A Promethean started its existence as some sort of machine: a construct that existed to serve its master and that lacked self-awareness and free will. At that stage in its existence, it wasn't a Promethean; it was just a tool.<br /> <br /> Then it encountered Prometheus, a force or entity that I view as being vaguely reminiscent of <b>Hunter</b>'s Messengers: no one has ever encountered it other than the constructs that it touches. When it touches a construct, it imbues that construct with the Spark, which in turn grants self-awareness and free will to it.<br /> <br /> A Promethean is a construct that has received the Spark.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's my point. It's not an analogue to Promethean. It's not a game line with its own stand alone intrinsic worth. It's just Mage adjacent. It's less separated from Mage than Mummy originally was from Vampire.<br /> <br /> It's not a real, robust line of supernaturals of its own. It's just dangling off Mage. Mage doesn't hang off Werewolf. There's some crossover. Same with Vampire and Wraith. And so on.<br /> <br /> Admittedly, it is going to be hard to not tie Wraith and Geist together pretty hardcore.... Though just stating &quot;Use Risen&quot; or &quot;Use Orpheus projectors&quot; doesn't really encompass the core ideas of Geist all that well. Orpheus projectors who have powers like Risen (&amp; Wraiths and... well, something like Euthanatos/necromancer Sorcerers) and have to deal with really Avatar-like Shadows... Almost seems more like Mummy....","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1062,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","user":"Ajax","date":". 01-02-2017, 08:24 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-02T20:09:32-08:00","id":1025689,"title":"","content":"Geist was among the concepts I actually really liked in NWoD. Interested me much more than Wraiths. Aside from stepping on toes, I'd like some kind of alternative in WoD with similar concepts. Maybe in the upcoming One Wod? Could be a new survival mechanic for Wraiths in the new metaplot and after the last great Maelstorm.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If nothing worked, then let's think!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6363-pm\u00e1rk","name":"PM\u00e1rk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6363_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2363"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-02T20:17:58-08:00","id":1025693,"title":"","content":"The reason I mentioned projectors is because, unlike the Risen, Sin-Eaters aren't dead. A Sin-Eater is a living human being who has become a sort of Uber-medium after a near-death experience. He's not a reanimated corpse; he's a living, breathing human who can interact with ghosts.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-02T21:39:20-08:00","id":1025721,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ajax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1024257-promethean-geist-and-beast-in-classic-world-of-darkness?p=1025634#post1025634\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That's my point. It's not an analogue to Promethean. It's not a game line with its own stand alone intrinsic worth. It's just Mage adjacent. It's less separated from Mage than Mummy originally was from Vampire.<br /> <br /> It's not a real, robust line of supernaturals of its own. It's just dangling off Mage. Mage doesn't hang off Werewolf. There's some crossover. Same with Vampire and Wraith. And so on.<br /> <br /> Admittedly, it is going to be hard to not tie Wraith and Geist together pretty hardcore.... Though just stating &quot;Use Risen&quot; or &quot;Use Orpheus projectors&quot; doesn't really encompass the core ideas of Geist all that well. Orpheus projectors who have powers like Risen (&amp; Wraiths and... well, something like Euthanatos/necromancer Sorcerers) and have to deal with really Avatar-like Shadows... Almost seems more like Mummy....</div> </div> </div> </div>Are you aware that there was no stand-alone Mummy game in the original World of Darkness? Ever? Every edition of that game, from the first-edition <b>World of Darkness: Mummy</b> through <b>Mummy: the Resurrection</b> required you to own the core book of another gameline. What's more, each edition incorporated elements from other gamelines, such as the Children of Osiris. True, these groups from other gamelines played supporting roles to the protagonists; but those were often <i>vital</i> roles, such as \u201cthe guys who completed your ritual of rebirth\u201d. <br /> <br /> With that context in mind: note that I never referenced <b>Mage</b> in my pitch. I mentioned <i>constructs</i>, but not mages. My thought is that it doesn't matter who made the construct, only that the construct lacks self-awareness and free will. Mage-made constructs are certainly one possibility; but they needn't be the only possibility. Does <b>Masquerade</b> include any sort of ability to make gargoyle-like constructs? If so, they'd be a potential target for Prometheus' Spark, too. I'd probably also include rituals for the Paths of Alchemy and Enchantment that would allow mortals to create constructs. It would be a bit more of a stretch, but I could also see including a Glasswalker Rite for investing spiritual energy into a puppet in order to animate it; <i>that</i> could count as a construct as far as Prometheus is concerned. <br /> <br /> In theory, the construct could come from anywhere; but it's not a Promethean until Prometheus intervenes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-03T09:16:08-08:00","id":1025974,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1024257-promethean-geist-and-beast-in-classic-world-of-darkness?p=1025721#post1025721\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Are you aware that there was no stand-alone Mummy game in the original World of Darkness? Ever? Every edition of that game, from the first-edition <b>World of Darkness: Mummy</b> through <b>Mummy: the Resurrection</b> required you to own the core book of another gameline. What's more, each edition incorporated elements from other gamelines, such as the Children of Osiris. True, these groups from other gamelines played supporting roles to the protagonists; but those were often <i>vital</i> roles, such as \u201cthe guys who completed your ritual of rebirth\u201d.<br /> <br /> With that context in mind: note that I never referenced <b>Mage</b> in my pitch. I mentioned <i>constructs</i>, but not mages. My thought is that it doesn't matter who made the construct, only that the construct lacks self-awareness and free will. Mage-made constructs are certainly one possibility; but they needn't be the only possibility. Does <b>Masquerade</b> include any sort of ability to make gargoyle-like constructs? If so, they'd be a potential target for Prometheus' Spark, too. I'd probably also include rituals for the Paths of Alchemy and Enchantment that would allow mortals to create constructs. It would be a bit more of a stretch, but I could also see including a Glasswalker Rite for investing spiritual energy into a puppet in order to animate it; <i>that</i> could count as a construct as far as Prometheus is concerned.<br /> <br /> In theory, the construct could come from anywhere; but it's not a Promethean until Prometheus intervenes.</div> </div> </div> </div>Take out the &quot;made by mages&quot; and substitute &quot;made by supernatural agency that is a another game line&quot;. That's the point. If you make Prometheans require Tremere making some replacement for the errant gargoyles or the Frankenstein creations of Etherites and Progenitors who have gone around the bend or uppity Mummy/Setite ushabtis or whatever. That makes it a dependent line, much like Mummy, as you point out. That's not what it is over in COD and that's not what the analogue supernaturals with their own lines are like in WOD. If you want a full-on line like Vampire through Demon, that's a cut below. Those lines have splats that cross over into the playgrounds of the other lines, but that's different than being a subset or a collection of by blows of the other lines. Not that that couldn't be a decent way to start conceptualizing a Promethean analogue, but there has got to be something more robust that characterizes the core supernatural that isn't dependent on other lines. Otherwise there's a lack of coherency. It's hard to see the various sub-parts having enough in common to really form a &quot;type&quot; of their own.<br /> <br /> Mummy, the last one, is an example of a line/quasi-line in the WOD that seems to share a lot of the traits with Sin-Eaters: They were dead. Something attached itself to them and that something is still with them (in Mummy it's the dominant personality and in Geist the human side is the persona with the &quot;other thing&quot; a lot like a Mages's Avatar... only slightly more coherent conceptually and thematically a little cooler for that reason). They are now back and alive. They have lots and lots of powers. Not that I think Mummy is/should be considered the WOD version of Geist, but it's a rough analogue along the axes. It's not thematically like Geist AT ALL. So it's, once again, not a great fit. But it's better than Risen, Orpheus, etc.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1062,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","user":"Ajax","date":". 01-03-2017, 02:36 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-06T15:21:31-08:00","id":1027868,"title":"","content":"Retracted Statement","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11693,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/","user":"Guest","date":". 02-13-2019, 08:42 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-06T17:02:53-08:00","id":1027923,"title":"","content":"I'd ditch the \u201cmight have been\u201d: they wouldn't have been, because the circumstances weren't right back when White Wolf was still making original World of Darkness gamelines. Instead, focus on \u201ccould be\u201d: assume for the sake of argument that White Wolf has authorized Onyx Path to make versions of their unique-to-ChroD gamelines but set in the original World of Darkness. I also wouldn't worry too much about making them fully stand-alone; my point with Mummy was that the original World of Darkness' counterpart to Mummy: the Curse is not a stand-alone gameline, and that's OK. Mummy sets a precedent.<br /> <br /> The key, I think, would lie in making the WoD versions distinct from their ChroD counterparts while still remaining recognizably similar. That's what I was trying for with my Promethean pitch: keep the notion of artificial beings on a journey from subhuman to something better, but shift the focus from \u201clearning to be human\u201d to \u201cgrowing up\u201d \u2014 gaining the independence to do your own thing, then developing the maturity to handle the responsibilities that come with said agency. That's why I was focusing on the \u201cPrometheus Spark\u201d being what separates a Promethean from a plain old ordinary artificial being: the Spark represents the agency that would set Prometheans apart from the artificial beings that already exist in the World of Darkness.<br /> <br /> Geist isn't going to be a stand-alone gameline, because its subject matter (life after death) is already covered by Wraith. True, Geist approaches it from almost the opposite able from Wraith; its protagonists are mediums and necromancers, living humans who interact with ghosts (thus their \u201cSin-Eater\u201d moniker); but they still exist in the same world as wraiths do: they have to deal with Stygia and its rules about non-interference between the living and dead. I proposed using Orpheus' projectors as a basis for this because they already exist in the original World of Darkness, but not in a way that's all that compatible with Wraith (so there's some room available to revise them); they already match the \u201cliving humans who are connected to death due to near-death experiences\u201d thing; and their core power (projecting their souls into the Shadowlands) would distinguish them from their ChroD counterparts. For this pitch, I'd call the protagonist's projected form his Geist. I wouldn't mess with the \u201ctwo minds\u201d thing; leave that with wraiths and the Risen. But let them cope with Spite in a manner similar to Orpheus' projectors.<br /> <br /> I haven't said much of anything about Beast because I don't really get it. I mean, I understand the concept more or less; but I don't get the appeal. As such, I'd never be able to do it justice.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-19T17:06:49-08:00","id":1034953,"title":"","content":"You can build off the stuff in Mage to work up some sort of &quot;World of Darkness: The Created&quot; or the like. Artificial beings empowered through seeming random chance to be walking quantum fluctuations trying to figure out their place in the universe. Or something like that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-19T18:20:56-08:00","id":1034979,"title":"","content":"Sorcerers can create artificial beings with Enchantment 5.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-24T18:14:29-08:00","id":1037534,"title":"","content":"So why not make all the gamelines just spinoffs from Mage? Werewolves are created by mages using Life and Spirit to make Garou. Vampires are just a mage death magic experiment gone awry (making the Tremere a sort of recidivist joke). Wraiths are mages stablilizing the spirits of dead and enabling them to have a post-biological life existence. Changelings are just mages grafting empowered dreams on human souls. Inspired are actually talking to their mage masters and using proxy mage magic....<br /> <br /> The independent or quasi-independent game lines do not dangle as accessories to extant lines. They just don't. Not even Mummy. They stand in their own right. There are crossovers and overlaps and places where they experience limited mergers, but there is a core conceit to the line that isn't just &quot;&lt;Insert name of full-on supernatural type&gt; is entirely the creation of &lt;Other type of supernatural&gt;&quot; If you want to equate Prometheans and Sin-Eaters to Kinfolk and Ghouls, subservient half-splats, then it makes perfect sense to say &quot;Geist Sin-Easters? Just Mediums.&quot; &quot;Prometheans? Just something Progenitors or Etherites cooked up in lab&quot;. In which case, the whole discussion is moot from the outset. The OP seems to be saying that they should be at least about the level of Mummy. (Which, I agree with Data, is pretty much the benchmark for an independent &quot;type&quot;).<br /> <br /> Otherwise, Sin-eaters need to be more than Mediums or Orpheus projectors. That doesn't capture the essence of Sin-Eaters and their Geists. Sin-Eaters, to be a Mummy-level type splat have got to have more to them than Risen. They need to take the idea of Sin-Eater, with something like a guiding spirit, the &quot;back from beyond&quot;, the essence of their Keys and Manifestations and then spin it in all inside the World of Darkness mythospace. Then follow out from that and make the changes. Mediums definitely don't have that. A Wraith20 projector might be a step closer, but, really, it seems like it's going to be &quot;Live Dude who's Live Dude power is being able to be Dead Dude/Dead Dude who pretty much = standard Wraith with a twist of lime&quot;. That doesn't encompass the very real power that Sin-Eater's have in the Skinlands.<br /> <br /> Soooo..... Hmmm...How about, instead of Orpheus projectors, take a spin off of the whole &quot;zombie&quot; thing that play initially in Hunter? When the Maelstrom/whatever happened that caused the issues that created the various types of the Walking Dead (oh and made the Mummy's do a phase/state change thing), there was something put in place that started shoving the souls of the departing back into their bodies with a huge surge of Shadowlands energy? I'd rather not have the &quot;Geist&quot; side of things be a specter that gets shoved in with... seems too much like a Mummy echo, or a fissure in the soul where &quot;Geist&quot; = &quot;Shadow&quot; in wraith terms, Geists are so cool, they echo the best ideas for Avatars - but... no, not that either, I think, since that makes Sin-eaters some kind of ur-mage. I'm stumped for now, but there seems like there's an idea to get a WoD version of a Geist in there somewhere.... In any case, you end up with a supernatural living human filled with usable death that can use that power. It's sourced in the WoD metaplot/setting.<br /> <br /> That's what I can come up with for now.... I'm going to chew on something that keeps Prometheans from being just an addendum to Mage..... There has got to be something with the Azoth thing.... I dunno. If there was some way for the Created to have come from multiple different game lines, where each game line had a way to create automata and then something FIRES some of them up.... That might work. But, really, it's just different types of mages, maybe vampires (yeah, a Promethean vozhd, now THAT would be fun...), but... not really the other lines. So that's a dead-ender.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-31T14:49:12-08:00","id":1041494,"title":"","content":"I know next to nothing of CoD... How does those Geist work?<br /> <br /> And what about Changelling the Lost? They should have a counterpart... Because, lets be honest, Changelling the Dreaming have nothing to do with the Lost, even if they use the words &quot;Arcadia&quot; and &quot;Fae&quot;, they are absolutely different kinds of critters.<br /> <br /> I never payed much attention to the New WoD, I didn't liked the new atlantean thing for Mage... And since I love Ascension... Well...<br /> <br /> But I gotta say, I just started looking at Wikia on the Lost... And I think I fell in love by this game. This is hard for me, since I love DA Fae and the Dreaming... But I want the Lost on my WoD...<br /> <br /> I was thinking... Maybe the Lost could be made with the Klapauss-something (the Cthulhu things from the beyond)?<br /> <br /> Also, I don't wanna destroy the Changellings from the Dreaming to place the Lost in their place","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12880-karlgust","name":"Karlgust","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"614"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-31T15:02:35-08:00","id":1041500,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1024257-promethean-geist-and-beast-in-classic-world-of-darkness?p=1025721#post1025721\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Are you aware that there was no stand-alone Mummy game in the original World of Darkness? Ever? Every edition of that game, from the first-edition <b>World of Darkness: Mummy</b> through <b>Mummy: the Resurrection</b> required you to own the core book of another gameline. What's more, each edition incorporated elements from other gamelines, such as the Children of Osiris. True, these groups from other gamelines played supporting roles to the protagonists; but those were often <i>vital</i> roles, such as \u201cthe guys who completed your ritual of rebirth\u201d. <br /> <br /> With that context in mind: note that I never referenced <b>Mage</b> in my pitch. I mentioned <i>constructs</i>, but not mages. My thought is that it doesn't matter who made the construct, only that the construct lacks self-awareness and free will. Mage-made constructs are certainly one possibility; but they needn't be the only possibility. Does <b>Masquerade</b> include any sort of ability to make gargoyle-like constructs? If so, they'd be a potential target for Prometheus' Spark, too. I'd probably also include rituals for the Paths of Alchemy and Enchantment that would allow mortals to create constructs. It would be a bit more of a stretch, but I could also see including a Glasswalker Rite for investing spiritual energy into a puppet in order to animate it; <i>that</i> could count as a construct as far as Prometheus is concerned. <br /> <br /> In theory, the construct could come from anywhere; but it's not a Promethean until Prometheus intervenes.</div> </div> </div> </div>I remember a &quot;Homunculus&quot; ritual from the Tremere I guess; Giovani can make &quot;zombies&quot;, and Tzimisce can make the Vozd-thing, I don't recall exactly the name now, things made of flesh<br /> <br /> But if we do that adaptation, maybe even snowmen made by humans could do... Statues, etc","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12880-karlgust","name":"Karlgust","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"614"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-31T15:09:02-08:00","id":1041505,"title":"","content":"And perhaps, chimerical creations maybe could linger on the real world after some changelling calling the Wyrd... And could become a prometean.<br /> <br /> And Wraiths can animate objects too... Their ectoplasmic ressonance could remain, and receive the spark.<br /> <br /> We could have different kinds of Prometeans according to origin - what would a chimerical construct that receives the spark and becomes real would be? And a construct infused with the energies of death?<br /> <br /> How about also, objects with awakened spirits from Fera?<br /> <br /> We could have<br /> <br /> Prometeans with vampiric blood<br /> Prometeans made of glamour<br /> Prometeans half spirit<br /> Prometeans of True Magik<br /> Prometeans infused with Death<br /> <br /> And maybe even, mundane ones, made by sleepers, just robots or statues","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12880-karlgust","name":"Karlgust","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"614"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-31T16:38:33-08:00","id":1041565,"title":"","content":"Chimera with the Wryd Rede can become real for a scene by spending just one point of Willpower, so powerful Chimera can just attack the real world before retreating back to the Dreaming. Potentially, some of the Chimera of the Far Dreaming and Deep Dreaming are powerful enough that they could end entire nations if they wished, but they dislike the feel of the banality too much to bother coming to the Autumn World unless they are really torqued off.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-31T19:17:18-08:00","id":1041636,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Karlgust</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1024257-promethean-geist-and-beast-in-classic-world-of-darkness?p=1041505#post1041505\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And perhaps, chimerical creations maybe could linger on the real world after some changelling calling the Wyrd... And could become a prometean.<br /> <br /> And Wraiths can animate objects too... Their ectoplasmic ressonance could remain, and receive the spark.<br /> <br /> We could have different kinds of Prometeans according to origin - what would a chimerical construct that receives the spark and becomes real would be? And a construct infused with the energies of death?<br /> <br /> How about also, objects with awakened spirits from Fera?<br /> <br /> We could have<br /> <br /> Prometeans with vampiric blood<br /> <b>Prometeans made of glamour</b><br /> Prometeans half spirit<br /> Prometeans of True Magik<br /> Prometeans infused with Death<br /> <br /> And maybe even, mundane ones, made by sleepers, just robots or statues</div> </div> </div> </div>Slight problem: Inanimae exist, and Manikins are one of their kiths.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-31T20:46:53-08:00","id":1041669,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1024257-promethean-geist-and-beast-in-classic-world-of-darkness?p=1041636#post1041636\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Slight problem: Inanimae exist, and Manikins are one of their kiths.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, not inanime, I'm talking about non sentient Chimera.<br /> <br /> Besides, it's just an idea.<br /> <br /> Well, we can also change the scenario just a bit to acomodate for that; for example, we could make Tremere, Giovanni and Tzimisce doing automatons a little more commonly; perhaps even Setites and Assamites too, hell, we could even make lasombra with that abyss mysticism; for example, having LVL 2 rituals for all those different paths that allow making simple servants. Taumaturgy 2 - golem. Necromancy 2 - zombie. Koldunism 2 - meat golem (for the others, it could be done similars too). Those servants would have no attack, no minds, useful mainly for domestic work, so they could be a very common feature of those vampires, meaning that a Tremere chantry would typically have 5-8 at least of them, a Giovanni would also have similar amounts of zombies, kolduns would keep those too to keep their houses etc.<br /> <br /> For the Fera, we could make it a common Gift, maybe for Ragabashs or Theurges, that allows the animation of matter, and those things would become a common sight on Caerns too.<br /> <br /> For wraiths, a new Arcanoi, maybe a new power of Insult, or another, that allows the same thing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12880-karlgust","name":"Karlgust","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"614"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-31T21:13:40-08:00","id":1041673,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Karlgust</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1024257-promethean-geist-and-beast-in-classic-world-of-darkness?p=1041500#post1041500\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I remember a &quot;Homunculus&quot; ritual from the Tremere I guess; Giovani can make &quot;zombies&quot;, and Tzimisce can make the Vozd-thing, I don't recall exactly the name now, things made of flesh<br /> <br /> But if we do that adaptation, maybe even snowmen made by humans could do... Statues, etc</div> </div> </div> </div>Snowmen and statues are inanimate. I suppose that the Spark could be granted to them, asking with mobility; but you'd lack the master/servant dynamic between their creators and themselves, which would clash with the dynamic I was suggesting. It's why I was aiming at constructs being animate entities lacking only self-determination. <br /> <br /> On the flip side: Inanimae Manikens, self-assured Progenitor clones, and similar artificial entities that already have free will wouldn't be candidates for Prometheus' Spark because they already have what it offers.<br /> <br /> Prometheans would exist in the gap between robots and golems that exist solely to serve their masters and artificially constructed beings who already have minds of their own.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-01T02:12:04-08:00","id":1041743,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1024257-promethean-geist-and-beast-in-classic-world-of-darkness?p=1041673#post1041673\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Snowmen and statues are inanimate. I suppose that the Spark could be granted to them, asking with mobility; but you'd lack the master/servant dynamic between their creators and themselves, which would clash with the dynamic I was suggesting. It's why I was aiming at constructs being animate entities lacking only self-determination. <br /> <br /> On the flip side: Inanimae Manikens, self-assured Progenitor clones, and similar artificial entities that already have free will wouldn't be candidates for Prometheus' Spark because they already have what it offers.<br /> <br /> Prometheans would exist in the gap between robots and golems that exist solely to serve their masters and artificially constructed beings who already have minds of their own.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, not inanime, when I said chimerical ones, I meant things like a Chimera who is a robot, or a Chimera who is a Can Man automaton and so, any chimerical automaton brought in the real world with calling the Wyrd... That by some reason, linger on in the material realm and receive the Spark.<br /> <br /> When I said snowmen and statues, I had one very specifics image in my mind: the Terracota men in China, that collection of thousands of statues of the fist emperor's tomb, in there to forever guard their master, and the archeologists believe his tomb is a huge piramid that became a Mountain. I was thinking that, despite not being real automatons, those guys have a huge psychic pulse on them; they are, in a figurative way, actively guarding the emperor in his eternal sleep. And in the WoD, that kind of thing have metaphysical strenght. So, I thou","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12880-karlgust","name":"Karlgust","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"614"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-01T04:45:11-08:00","id":1041764,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Karlgust</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1024257-promethean-geist-and-beast-in-classic-world-of-darkness?p=1041494#post1041494\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I know next to nothing of CoD... How does those Geist work?</div> </div> </div> </div>Geists began as ghosts, but they've lost a lot of their own identity and become more like a facet of a particular archetype of death. CoD ghosts don't have an equivalent of a wraith's shadow, and geists are pretty monstrous - so in Wraith terms, a geist is easiest to conceptualise as <i>both</i> the psyche and shadow losing their identities in favour of an exaggerated representation of how the wraith originally died, and kinda merging - how that would happen in Wraith's lands of the dead is open to question (in Geist, the Underworld has a lot of big rivers running through it, and ghosts become geists when they drink from them).<br /> <br /> The actual protagonists of Geist aren't the geists though. They are sineaters, who at the moment of their deaths have been offered possession by a geist. If they accept, the geist merges with their psyche and resurrects them. (It can do this again, if they get killed, though doing so too much damages how well the two are merged). Life-cycle-wise, it's probably more comparable to Mummy the Resurrection than anything else. Sineaters have powerful necromantic abilities, the ability to visit the Underworld, and a culture that heavily celebrates life.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And what about Changelling the Lost? They should have a counterpart... Because, lets be honest, Changelling the Dreaming have nothing to do with the Lost, even if they use the words &quot;Arcadia&quot; and &quot;Fae&quot;, they are absolutely different kinds of critters. </div> </div> </div>Changeling the Lost is probably most comparable to Kindred of the East among OWoD games. The PC's have been snatched away into a pretty hellish realm (unlike KotE, they don't have to die for this to happen, and it doesn't have to be their fault) - they've escaped, at the cost of their soul being slashed up, and obviously being turned into supernatural beings. The Fae and Arcadia do have a lot of the dream logic that Changeling the Dreaming has, though.<br /> <br /> If I had to make a suggestion about having both games, it would be blending their mythoi rather than trying to have both independent. Lost has a realm called the Hedge, which is an intermediate realm between Earth and Arcadia. It has its own inhabitants, known collectively as hobgoblins, which ... well, you said you've been looking at the wiki, so you probably know all this. So, ok, my suggestions:<br /> <br /> 1. Conflate the Hedge and the dreamscape that Dreaming changelings can visit - it's still inhabited by hobgoblins (while I'm calling it the Hedge in this list, make it look more like Dreaming's dreamscape).<br /> 2. Arcadia lies beyond it - from a human perspective, it conforms to the hellish Arcadia of Lost, but it might be more habitable for hobgoblins - it's still ruled over by Gentry.<br /> 3. There was a &quot;shattering&quot; event as in Dreaming, which made it harder to travel between Earth, the Hedge, and Arcadia. This also left too much banality on Earth and too much bedlam in Arcadia.<br /> 4. Most Dreaming-changelings are hobgoblins who were trapped on Earth after this event, but have adapted to life there. They can call on the nature of the Hedge and create their chimerical reality on Earth.<br /> 5. Dreaming's sidhe are <i>Gentry</i> who were similarly stranded.<br /> 6. Lost-changelings are humans pulled into Arcadia by Gentry in their attempt to counter its bedlam - but some escape.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/321-sunlessnick","name":"SunlessNick","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-01T06:52:32-08:00","id":1041793,"title":"","content":"Well, the Arcadian Mages (the souls of the mortals who bodies the sidhe claimed) are probably the closest parallel to CtL. The problem is the conflicting tone of the two games. In CtD, the Dreaming is a source of wonder, and Arcadia is the lost homeland that all changeling unconsciously seek to regain. In CtL, it is very much the opposite.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-01T09:24:30-08:00","id":1041870,"title":"","content":"CtL has something in it called Charlatans: Gentry who have been kicked out of Arcadia and trapped in man's world. They desperately want to go home. They're not a perfect fit for CtD-style changelings; but they're surprisingly close\u2014close enough that I could see replacing them with CtD-style changelings in a merger setting. <br /> <br /> I consider CtD and CtL to be counterpart games in the two settings; but it's similar to how DtF and DtD are counterparts: there's enough in common that concepts and mechanics from each one can be ported over into the other; but there are enough core differences between each game's protagonists that you can't reasonably devise a hybrid of the two. Still, if they were able to manage a Demon Translation Guide, I see no reason why a Changeling Translation Guide would be impossible.<br /> <br /> This is especially true with CtL2e: many of the changes from 1e to 2e make the game more similar to CtD. Kiths and Seemings are separate things; CtL2e's Hedge is more Dreaming-like; and so on. <br /> <br /> Admittedly, the two games' concepts of Seemings are very different. From CtD's perspective, CtL's protagonists are all Grumps; and from CtL's perspective, CtD's protagonists have no need for CtL-style Seemings. <br /> <br /> And there are some surprising parallels between the two: most notably, Banality and Clarity almost literally parallel each other, with high ratings representing an attunement of sorts with the mortal world. Where they differ is whether this is a good thing (Clarity) or a bad thing (Banality). For a hybrid game, I'd probably use Banality as a baseline, but integrate elements of Clarity into it so that it represents more of a mixed bag instead of leaning so heavily one way or the other. <br /> <br /> I once started doing a homebrew CTG, back before the original White Wolf morphed into Onyx Path. I've put that project on hold until both CtL2e and CtD20 are out; but I've got a lot of ideas about how to draw connections between them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}